Chess Amateur probe instrumentation patch for Stockfish sf_17.

This patch adds a single, minimal UCI emission inside the "Step 5. Tablebases
probe" block of src/search.cpp. When Stockfish is about to probe the Syzygy
tablebases for a position it is SEARCHING (i.e. the piece count / depth /
rule50 / castling guards already decided a probe is warranted) but the probe
FAILS because the tablebase is not loaded or insufficient
(err == TB::ProbeState::FAIL), the engine prints the distinctive UCI line:

    info string CA_TB_ABOUT_TO_PROBE

The Chess Amateur app reads the raw UCI stream (engine.py::_uci_log) and uses
this marker to detect that a tablebase probe WOULD have occurred for a searched
endgame position while the tablebases are still downloading, so it can defer the
move until the download completes.

Design notes:
  * The marker fires ONLY on err == TB::ProbeState::FAIL, so when the tablebase
    IS present (probe succeeds) nothing is emitted -> no UCI spam in normal play.
  * The existing `if (err != TB::ProbeState::FAIL)` branch (which uses the WDL
    result and can prune/return) is left completely untouched, so search results
    are identical to stock Stockfish. This block is pure instrumentation.
  * The guard conditions of the enclosing `if` already ensure this is a
    position Stockfish is SEARCHING (not merely the current/root board), and
    that its piece count is within the probe cardinality -- exactly the
    "about to probe" moment required.
  * sync_cout / sync_endl are Stockfish's thread-safe UCI output convention and
    are already used elsewhere in this same file (search.cpp).

diff --git a/src/search.cpp b/src/search.cpp
--- a/src/search.cpp
+++ b/src/search.cpp
@@ -643,6 +643,17 @@
         {
             TB::ProbeState err;
             TB::WDLScore   wdl = Tablebases::probe_wdl(pos, &err);
+
+            // Chess Amateur probe instrumentation.
+            // A probe was attempted for this SEARCHED position (the piece
+            // count / depth / rule50 / castling guards above already decided a
+            // probe is warranted) but it FAILED because the tablebase is not
+            // loaded or insufficient. Emit a distinctive UCI marker so the app
+            // can detect "about to probe but tablebase absent" while the Syzygy
+            // download is still in progress. Fires only on FAIL, so it never
+            // spams when the tablebase is present, and it does not alter search.
+            if (err == TB::ProbeState::FAIL)
+                sync_cout << "info string CA_TB_ABOUT_TO_PROBE" << sync_endl;
 
             // Force check of time on the next occasion
             if (is_mainthread())
